<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">A hand-typed test fixture is a frozen guess about the API's shape from the day it was written — nothing checks it against reality, so it can drift silently until production breaks.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">MSW intercepts the real network call your component already makes, and pairing it with a shared schema turns a shape mismatch into a loud CI failure instead of a silent production one.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">The schema has to be the real contract, generated from or validated against the backend's actual spec, not a second hand-written guess — and run the same contract tests on backend PRs too, not just frontend ones.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
